1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,327
There was a number.

2
00:00:02,367 --> 00:00:04,389
More than eleven hundred.

3
00:00:04,429 --> 00:00:06,038
Two hundred in Iran.

4
00:00:06,078 --> 00:00:10,410
Ninety-one in Lebanon. Four
in Israel. One in Kuwait.

5
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:15,523
The report had no names in it.
Only numbers. Numbers are tidy.

6
00:00:15,563 --> 00:00:17,585
Children's names are not.

7
00:00:17,625 --> 00:00:19,977
In Isfahan, Zahra was twelve.

8
00:00:20,017 --> 00:00:25,585
She fell on a stairwell while running
for shelter and hurt her head.

9
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:28,307
It wasn't a missile. It was fear.

10
00:00:28,347 --> 00:00:30,616
In Nabatieh, Youssef is six.

11
00:00:30,656 --> 00:00:34,493
He is alive, but his right
ear no longer hears.

12
00:00:34,533 --> 00:00:38,039
Children don't know why
anyone is fighting.

13
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:39,771
Adults think they do.

14
00:00:39,811 --> 00:00:43,275
That difference is what makes all of this.
